+# Independent all-sector connectivity review
+
+PASS for corrected proof4c75aa744eebf8f086a183aecc8ff14459f12827bdc0571fca2e29a35cbc7aa8, with the stated conditional support-graph scope. Original750a6671 was read completely together with complete check.py. Its only requested correction was the final Hamiltonian coefficient qualifier: real coefficients must be nonzero on every available edge. Root preserved the old bytes and made that exact change. Distinct edge flips have distinct target bitstrings, so they cannot cancel in the sum.
+
+Independently rederived the directed cut identity: outdegree−indegree=2Q, hence summing on a reachable set with no outgoing boundary arrows gives nonpositive2sumQ. A positive starting vertex and no negative in that set contradict this. A simple path exists; truncating before the first negative and after the last positive makes its interior neutral. Sequential reversals transport+ and annihilate at−, so D drops exactly2, with no forbidden intermediate. At mostV−1 edges per pair gives the reduction bound. The argument uses the whole available low domain; it does not apply to T-only/D-conserving support or a further restricted winding/cycle sector.
+
+For two ice orientations, changed outgoing and incoming counts agree at each vertex. Their difference therefore decomposes into directed simple cycles. Reversing one cycle via an ephemeral pair stays in low charge and preserves all other edge orientations; its intermediate vertices are distinct. All changed edges are used once, giving at mostE. Reversing the reduction of the target gives the displayed full bound. The Eulerian existence claim is valid for finite even-regular graphs. Bipartiteness supplies the original bit-to-charge orientation dictionary, not an unproved combinatorial expansion condition. No min-cut-six premise is needed.
+
+Independent controls use K6,6, not the author's L4 graph: ten fixed configurations including D=0 andD=12, all100 ordered source/target routes, exact intermediate charges and length bounds. No author code or fixtures were imported. A literal native ordered-star phase wordabcabc from a degree-three ice configuration also has phase−1 while all intermediates stay low. This independently corroborates the phase obstruction, not just support reachability. Full raw routes and states are in RESULT.json. These are finite controls, not enumeration of all2^36 orientations.
+
+The source correctly excludes Perron positivity, mixing/gap estimates and physical formation. Its off-D operator dictionary requires an independent phase theorem, since optional D-block phases no longer cancel. Connectivity neither creates an independent matter factor nor identifies the old Noether charge. A diagonal gauge cannot erase the closed−1 phase, but this does not rule out a general non-diagonal unitary. No further correction requested.
